# prose-audit: Grade A — The Oder disaster is carried by river towns, regulators, industry and the German border, with every response distinguishing evidence, authority and political ownership.
title: Mass fish deaths in the Oder
face-image: img/poland/events/oder-disaster-2022.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: odra_2022_done = 1; climate_state_capacity -= 4; public_trust -= 2; pis_poll_momentum -= 0.4; news_headline = "Mass fish deaths expose a failure of warning and response"

= August 2022 — A visible failure of regulation

Tonnes of dead fish appear along the Oder before central authorities can give
river towns a reliable warning. **Polish Waters**, environmental inspectorates,
industrial users and regional governments hold different pieces of the record;
communities downstream receive the consequences before they receive an agreed
explanation. German authorities across the river are investigating the same
water under another chain of command.

Lewica can pursue the evidence, build local response capacity, internationalise
the inquiry or reduce the catastrophe to another ministerial scandal. Those
choices will decide whether anything remains after the culprit leaves the news.

